+## 10. Merge attempt result (2026-10-16, final): gate fails; wholesale merge abandoned
+
+I resolved all 35 conflicts (taking main's side where main's change was the later,
+deliberate one, e.g. `ea9a7648` outbox semantics; keeping release-line additive
+files such as board-13 `src/grants/policy/*`; deleting the release's flattened
+test-fixture duplicates; re-pinning the locked policy) and committed the merge as
+`4d2db617`. The full gate then FAILED at the merged head: `npm run check` → **53
+lint errors across 16 files**, including:
+
+- a file the earlier agent had staged **still containing conflict markers**
+  (`src/backend/features/islands/tests/harness.ts`, with duplicated imports);
+- parsing errors in release-added files (`chatabuse/devicerevoke/tests/order.test.ts`,
+  `fixture/devicerevoke/tests/order.test.ts`);
+- 40+ `no-unsafe-*` "error typed value" failures cascading from cross-line type
+  resolution (`devicerevoke/index.ts`, `views/admin/DefaultsView.tsx`,
+  `views/admin/defaultApply.tsx`, `shell/view/defaults.ts`, admin test files);
+- three `max-lines-per-file` violations (51/52 code lines).
+
+Conclusion (final): the wholesale release→main merge is **not a bounded task**.
+Beyond the conflicts, the two lines' *non-conflicting* additions do not integrate
+cleanly (release-added modules fail to typecheck against main's code), and the
+prior partial resolution left corrupt files. Completing it needs a dedicated,
+careful front with a full clean redo and a green gate — or a decision that main
+has superseded the release line.
+
+Abandoned: the broken merge commit is local-only (`integration/195-release-onto-main`
+@ `4d2db617`, clone `/workspace/agent-195-integration/repo`); **nothing pushed**.
+Recommend the Founder/parliament decide between a dedicated integration front and
+closing #195 as superseded; recommend against further ad-hoc merge attempts.
